    "summary_one_sentence": "Grieving the loss of her sister, an aspiring San Francisco baker leaves hilariously honest voicemails on her late sister's phone, unaware that the reassigned recipient—a charming real estate agent—is listening and falling in love with her.",
    "summary_short": "Following the tragic loss of her sister Isabelle to cystic fibrosis, San Francisco resident Jill copes with her grief by leaving candid, funny voicemails on her sister's old phone number. Unbeknownst to Jill, the number has been reassigned to Wes, an Austin-based real estate agent who finds himself deeply drawn to her raw honesty and humor. Intrigued by her confessions, Wes travels to California to track her down, sparking an undeniable real-world connection between them. However, as their bond grows, Wes must confront the difficult truth of how he discovered her and risk losing the love he found.",
    "summary_long": "Aspiring San Francisco baker Jill struggles to pick up the pieces of her life after her younger sister, Isabelle, dies from cystic fibrosis. To cope with her overwhelming grief and process her chaotic dating experiences, Jill routinely dials Isabelle's old mobile number to leave unfiltered, hilarious voicemails. Unbeknownst to her, the phone number has been reassigned to Wes, a real estate agent living in Austin, Texas. As Wes listens to Jill's vulnerable confessions, he quickly becomes captivated by her personality and finds himself falling in love from afar. Driven by a desire to meet her, Wes arranges a work trip to San Francisco and orchestrates a meeting with Jill without revealing how he knows her. The two hit it off immediately, exploring the city together and forming a deep, genuine connection as Jill opens up about her dreams. Their blooming romance hits a wall when Jill attends a wedding with Wes and accidentally discovers that his phone is receiving her call to Isabelle. Devastated and feeling betrayed by his deception, Jill angrily breaks things off to throw herself into opening a dessert taco food truck. Determined to make amends, Wes leaves her a heartfelt voicemail on New Year's Eve explaining how much she means to him and preserving her sister's line. Touched by his sincerity, Jill forgives Wes, allowing them to reconcile and build a genuine future together.",
    "synopsis": "Voicemails for Isabelle is a romantic comedy-drama that centers on Jill, a passionate young woman in San Francisco attempting to navigate grief, career setbacks, and modern dating following the loss of her sister Isabelle. Struggling to move on, Jill uses her sister's inactive phone number as a personal diary, leaving candid and humorous voicemails to process her feelings. The narrative shifts when the line is reassigned to Wes, an Austin-based real estate agent who finds comfort and intrigue in her daily messages. As Wes decides to seek out the woman behind the voice, the story explores themes of love, healing, and sisterly bonds, delivering a heartwarming blend of humor and emotional resonance.",
